(178, 1, 9, 57, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Fanget i en pattedyrsskure', 'Trapped in a mammal shed', 'The compound word \'pattedyrsskure\' isn\'t one that\'s used in Danish, but its component words \'pattedyrs\' and \'skure\' mean \'mammal\' and \'shed\', respectively. Presumably they were trying to convey the same idea of being stuck on a certain train of thought.'),
