(220, 1, 11, 77, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Gravitationellt otursförföljd', 'Gravitationally misfortunate ', 'This is a reference to Johnny Vegas\' charity appeal video for the \"less gravitationally fortunate\", in the \'Make the best upside-down film\' task.'),
(221, 1, 11, 77, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Rotationspunkt', 'Rotation point', NULL),
(222, 1, 11, 78, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Hyllynpylly', NULL, '\'Hyllynpylly\' is apparently a nonsense word; the closest word to it, \'hyllypylly\', basically means \'lardass\'.'),
(223, 1, 11, 78, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Utmaning utan mottagning', 'Challenge without reception', 'This title is catchier in Swedish, because it rhymes. It\'s unclear what it might be a reference to - perhaps the \'Make the phone ring\' task?'),
(224, 1, 11, 78, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Det rene pladder', 'It\'s pure jabber', 'In Danish, to say that someone \'pladdrar\' means that they\'re talking nonsense.'),
(225, 1, 11, 79, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Vihaan lenkkareitasi', 'I hate your trainers', NULL),
(226, 1, 11, 79, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Statiskt mobilt måleri', 'Static mobile painting', 'This is a reference to the \'Paint a howling wolf on a rotating teapot\' task.'),
(227, 1, 11, 79, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Jeg hader dine kondisko', 'I hate your sneakers', 'Danish has two words for sports shoes, which correspond to the English words \'sneakers\' and \'trainers\'. \'Kondisko\' translates to \'sneakers\'.'),
(228, 1, 11, 80, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Virtahepo', 'Hippopotamus', NULL),
(229, 1, 11, 80, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Tysta drinken börjar nu!', 'Quietest drink starts now!', 'This is wordplay on \'Quietest play starts now\', the non-game that parents set their children, to get five minutes of peace. It\'s also referencing the \'Quietly make a cocktail\' task.'),
(230, 1, 11, 80, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Flodhest', 'Hippopotamus', NULL),
(231, 1, 11, 81, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Oikeaa lasia', 'Legit glass', NULL),
(232, 1, 11, 81, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Kassettband, kassaskåp och kassa lösningar', 'Cassette tapes, safes, and horrible solutions', 'This is a reference to the \'Communicate the safe contents via reversed audio\' task. All of the words in Swedish begin with \'kass\', which also means \'bad\'. Although the literal translation of the word \'kassa\' is \'cash\', it is also a slang word meaning \'horrible\'.\r\n\r\n'),
(233, 1, 11, 81, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Ægte glas', 'Real glass', NULL),
(234, 1, 11, 82, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Hiljaisia hetkiä', 'Silent moments', NULL),
(235, 1, 11, 82, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Mordgåta med manusminnesförlust', 'Murder mystery with script amnesia', 'This is a reference to the \'Learn your lines and perform a scene\' task.'),
(236, 1, 11, 82, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Stille øjeblikke', 'Silent moments', NULL),
(237, 1, 11, 83, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Äänitorvi-Andy', 'Air Horn Andy', NULL),
(238, 1, 11, 83, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Se upp för dårarna - dörrarna stängs', 'Watch out for fools - the doors are closing', 'There\'s a movie named <em>Se upp för dårarna</em>, to which this could be a reference. It is otherwise referencing the \'Complete the most tasks behind the five motorised doors\' task.'),
(239, 1, 11, 83, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Andy Tågehorn', 'Andy Foghorn', NULL),
(240, 1, 11, 84, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Koiranmakkaratorttu', 'Dog sausage tart', NULL),
(241, 1, 11, 84, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Kakafonisk karaoke', 'Cacophony karaoke', 'This is a reference to the \'Complete the best performance of a specific song\' task.'),
(242, 1, 11, 84, 'Denmark', 'TV2 Play', 'Hundemadstrifli', 'Dog food trifle', NULL),
(243, 1, 32, 211, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Se ei ole sinun syytäsi', 'It\'s not your fault', NULL),
(244, 1, 32, 211, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Säg hej till balalajkan', 'Say hello to the balalaika', 'This is most likely referencing the 1980s ventriloquism sketch by Johannes Brost and Per Eggers, known as \'Säg hej till publiken\', or \'Say hello to the audience\'. It\'s also a reference to the \'Do something impressive under the table while waving\' task, particularly Mike Wozniak\'s attempt.'),
(245, 1, 32, 212, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Siirappisten koiranpentujen houkutus', 'The lure of syrupy puppies', NULL),
(246, 1, 32, 212, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Skräck och ballångest', 'Horror and balloon-anxiety', 'This is a reference to the \'Make the house haunted\' and \'Make the balloon hover\' tasks. \'Ballångest\' is a punny portmanteau on the words \'ballong\' (balloon) and \'ångest\' (anxiety), since \'ong\' and \'ång\' sound the same, in this context.'),
(247, 1, 32, 213, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Puuta pitkin kuuhun', 'Up a tree to the moon', NULL),
(248, 1, 32, 213, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Säkerhetskontroll utom kontroll', 'Security check out of control', 'This is a reference to the \'Get your luggage through security\' task.'),
(249, 1, 32, 214, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Ennenaikainen hevoskastanja', 'Premature horse-chestnut', NULL),
(250, 1, 32, 214, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Full rulle med toarulle', 'Full roll with loo roll', 'This is a reference to the \'Get the sheet of loo roll as far away as possible\' task. \'Full rulle\' is a Swedish expression meaning \'full speed\', but also refers to a full toilet roll, in this context.'),
(251, 1, 32, 215, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Pihdit ojoon', 'Tongs outstretched', NULL),
(252, 1, 32, 215, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Den lilla tejpjungfrun', 'The little tape-mermaid', 'This is a reference to the \'Cover your legs in cling film and gaffer tape / Put on the captain’s hat\' task. Note: In Bäst i Test\'s adaptation of this task, the second part of the task instructs the contestants to recreate Den lille Havfrue (The Little Mermaid), a bronze statue of a mermaid in Copenhagen, Denmark.'),
(253, 1, 32, 216, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Sekametelisoppa', 'Hotchpotch', NULL),
(254, 1, 32, 216, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'En förrädisk fis', 'A treacherous fart', 'This is a reference to Mike Wozniak\'s unfortunate experience during the \'Fart\' task.'),
(255, 1, 32, 217, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Tuskaa ja maatuskaa', 'Pain and matryoshka dolls', 'Unclear what the \'pain\' part is referencing, but the matroyshka dolls are clearly a reference to the \'Make the best babushka meal\' task. The title is punny in Finnish, since both words end in \'tuskaa\'.'),
(256, 1, 32, 217, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Den stora babushka-banketten', 'The great babushka banquet', 'This is a reference to the \'Make the best babushka meal\' task.'),
(257, 1, 32, 218, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Järjestelmällinen laji', 'A systematic species', NULL),
(258, 1, 32, 218, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Säg metronom som ett fån', 'Say metronome like a fool', 'This is a reference to the \'Complete various tasks while saying \"metronome\"\' task. In Swedish, the words \'metronom\' and \'fån\' <em>almost</em> rhyme.'),
(259, 1, 32, 219, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Herra Mustekala ja Pottakäsi', 'Mr Octopus and Pottyhands', NULL),
(260, 1, 32, 219, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Orosmolnen tornar upp sig', 'The clouds of worry are gathering', 'This is presumably a reference to the \'Make the most impressive weather for Taskmaster Island\' task.'),
(261, 1, 32, 220, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Finaali', 'Finale', 'This appears to just be a reference to the fact that it is the season finale, though they haven\'t taken this approach on the other seasons of the show available on the streaming service.'),
(262, 1, 32, 220, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Kopiatorus Rex', 'Copiersaurus Rex', 'This is a reference to the \'Make the best picture of a big, scary dinosaur\' task.'),
(263, 1, 38, 262, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Poksahtavuuden epätasapaino', 'An imbalance in the poppability', NULL),
(264, 1, 38, 262, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Saxen och poppsnöret', 'The scissors and the pop-string', 'The \'pop-string\' here is a reference to the string which had to be cut to drop the portcullis on the balloon, during the \'Pop the balloon\' task. The word \'popsnöre\' is usually used to refer to young pop musicians or pop music fans, though.'),
(265, 1, 38, 263, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Kaurapuuroa ja kuolemaa', 'Oatmeal and death', NULL),
(266, 1, 38, 263, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Mount Evetest', 'Mount Evertask', 'Just a pun on \'Mount Everest\', in reference to the \'Scale the mountain\' task, incorporating the word \'test\', which is used when referring to the tasks.'),
(267, 1, 38, 264, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Bond-leffojen tuho', 'The destruction of Bond movies', NULL),
(268, 1, 38, 264, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Irriterande repeterande kopierande', 'Annoying repetitive copying', 'These Swedish words rhyme, and are referring to the \'Copy Alex\' task.'),
(269, 1, 38, 265, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Kustomoitu inhalaattori', 'A customised inhaler', NULL),
(270, 1, 38, 265, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Att vara helt ute och cykla', 'To be completely out and cycling', 'The phrase \'Att vara helt ute och cykla\' is a Swedish expression used to describe someone who\'s completely lost (mentally-speaking), in somewhat the same way that we might figuratively describe someone as \'lost at sea\' in English. Many Swedes cycle to let their minds drift, and therefore joke about being absent-minded when they are cycling. In this case, the phrase is clearly a reference to contestants\' struggles during the \'Complete the course as slowly as possible\' task.'),
(271, 1, 38, 266, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Kroissantti on kroisssantti', 'A croissant is a croissant', NULL),
(272, 1, 38, 266, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Tårtbak och baklängesmål', 'Cake baking and backwards goal', 'The title is referencing the cake-baking which occurs in the \'Sit on a cake\' task, and the goalpost-reversing that happens during the \'Prevent Alex from scoring a goal\' task.'),
(273, 1, 38, 267, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Tuoli karkin sisällä', 'A chair inside a candy', NULL),
(274, 1, 38, 267, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Vovvar och cirklar', 'Pooches and circles', 'This title is simply referencing the \'Make a cute toy for a cute dog\' task and the circular mats used in the \'Sit on the red chair in the secret tower\' task. The two Swedish words also rhyme, which makes it catchier.'),
(275, 1, 38, 268, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Tuotteen eheys', 'Integrity of the product', NULL),
(276, 1, 38, 268, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Snooker, rör och snokar i rör', 'Snooker, pipes, and snakes in pipes', 'The title is referencing the snooker balls in the \'Put up a shelf for the Taskmaster\'s snooker balls\' task, the pipe in the \'Pass everything through the pipe and the pipe through everything\' task, and the small canned snakes in the \'Write and perform a 30-second jingle\' task. The word \'snok\' is normally used to refer to a small type of snake typically found in bushes (the word used for snakes more generally is \'orm\').'),
(277, 1, 38, 269, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Pari Etheliä', 'A couple of Ethels', NULL),
(278, 1, 38, 269, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Du får inte undvika att inte missa det här', 'You must not avoid to not miss this', 'This title is simply referencing the confusing multiple negative clauses used in the task brief for the \'Make a popcorn necklace and do the right thing\' task.'),
(279, 1, 38, 270, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Millään ei ole väliä', 'Nothing matters', NULL),
(280, 1, 38, 270, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Telefonlurendrejerier', 'Phone trickery', 'This title is referencing the deceptive nature of the phonecalls, during the \'Have the longest telephone conversation\' task.'),
(281, 1, 38, 271, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Huolehtiva Minpict-setä', 'Caring Uncle Minpict', NULL),
(282, 1, 38, 271, 'Sweden', 'SVT Play', 'Saftiga frierier', 'Juicy proposals', 'This title is referencing both the \'Drink with your mouth open\' and \'Propose to Alex\' tasks. The word \'saftiga\' (\'juicy\') is carrying a double meaning here, referring both to the fruit squash (\'saft\' is a type of berry juice drink), and the proposals to Alex being \'juicy\' (as in \'scandalous\' or \'appealing\').'),
(283, 1, 48, 312, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Sinisestä lähtevä ääni', 'The noise that blue makes', NULL),
(284, 1, 48, 313, 'Finland', 'MTV Katsomo', 'Lintukäsisormi', 'Birdy hand finger', NULL),
